<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Carlson Trophic State Index from chlorophyll-a (fixed 0-100 scale, even 5-unit steps): <b>0-35</b> Oligotrophic (deep blue&rarr;green, chl 0.04-1.62) &rarr; <b>40-45</b> Mesotrophic (yellow-green, chl 2.6-4.1) &rarr; <b>50-60</b> Eutrophic (gold&rarr;red-orange, chl 6.4-20) &rarr; <b>65-100</b> Hypereutrophic (red&rarr;violet&rarr;dark, chl 31-1183). Legend labels show TSI (chl-a ug/L). Same TSI always shows the same color. High TSI = biomass / activity, not toxins.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Chlorophyll.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>21600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
